-- title:
--   A generator of H²(P,C_F) with prescribed local restrictions
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $F/E$ be a Galois extension of number fields, and let $D$ be an idèle Galois descent datum for $(\mathcal{O}_F, E, F)$, i.e. a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ to the ring automorphisms of the adèle ring of $F$ which is continuous in each $g$ and compatible with $F \to \mathbb{A}_F$. Assume the idèle class group $C_F = (\mathbb{A}_F)^\times / \mathrm{principalIdeles}$ carries a multiplicative-distributive action of $\mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ agreeing with the one induced by $D$ on quotients (`hact`). Assume given, for each height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_F$, a homomorphism $\iota_w : (F_w)^\times \to (\mathbb{A}_F)^\times$ producing concentrated idèles ($w$-component $x$, all other finite components and the infinite part $1$), and a morphism $\lambda_w$ of $\mathbb{Z}$-representations of the decomposition subgroup $D_w = \mathrm{decomp}\,E\,F\,w$ from $(F_w)^\times$ to the restriction of $C_F$ along $D_w \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$, sending $x$ to the class of $\iota_w(x)$. Let $P \le \mathrm{Gal}(F/E)$ be a $p$-group. Then there is $u_P \in H^2(P, C_F)$ whose $\mathbb{Z}$-span is all of $H^2(P, C_F)$, such that for every $w$ the following holds for every local comparison datum: a prime $q$, a finite extension $L'$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure, carrying a $D_w$-action by semiring automorphisms and a compatible action on $(L')^\times$, a ring isomorphism $\Phi : F_w \cong L'$ that is $D_w$-equivariant, with $D_w$ acting trivially on $\mathbb{Q}_q$-scalars; a finite extension $K_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ which is a base for $(L', D_w)$, that is $K_0 \le L'$ and an element of $L'$ lies in $K_0$ exactly when it is fixed by all of $D_w$; a morphism $\theta$ of $D_w$-representations from $(L')^\times$ to $(F_w)^\times$ inducing $\Phi^{-1}$ on underlying elements; and a class $u' \in H^2(D_w, (L')^\times)$ satisfying the predicate [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsLocalFundamentalClass`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L60), which pins $u'$ down by demanding that for every unramified overlay datum (a larger finite extension $M \supseteq L'$ with a finite group $H$ acting faithfully, normal subgroups $N_L, N_n$, an isomorphism $D_w \cong H/N_L$, a Frobenius lift $\varphi$ and a uniformiser $\pi$ satisfying the listed fixed-field, Frobenius and valuation conditions) together with a compatible inclusion of representations, the pullback of $u'$ to $H^2(H, M^\times)$ equals the inflation of the class of the cyclic carry $2$-cocycle built from $\varphi$ and $\pi$. Namely, the image of $u'$ under $H^2(\theta)$ followed by $H^2(\lambda_w)$, restricted from $D_w$ to $D_w \sqcap P$ along the inclusion, equals the restriction of $u_P$ from $P$ to $D_w \sqcap P$, both computed in $H^2(D_w \sqcap P, C_F)$.
--
--   This is the $p$-subgroup form of the statement that $H^2(P, C_F)$ is infinite cyclic (as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, generated by $u_P$) on the fundamental class of the layer $F/F^P$, normalised by the requirement that its restrictions to the groups $D_w \sqcap P$ are the images of the local fundamental classes under the concentrated-idèle maps $\lambda_w$. It is the form of the global fundamental class used downstream, being cited by [`M4aHerbrand.exists_unit_forall_exists_localFundamentalClass_eq_smul_res_and_pow_dvd_of_ne_two`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_unit_forall_exists_localFundamentalClass_eq_smul_res_and_pow_dvd_of_ne_two); the restriction to odd $p$ reflects the behaviour at the infinite places in the route taken here.
